{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1199609-the-evolution-of-banes-and-possession","id":1199609,"title":"The Evolution of Banes and Possession","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-25T23:44:51-07:00","id":1199609,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> The Evolution of Banes and Possession","content":"So something I feel wasn't touched upon enough is the effect of Possession on Banes. I don't like the default of assumption of Banes being static and interchangeable. I feel banes start out often pretty homogeneous but the process of possession fundamentally changes a bane. I feel at that point a bane is forever unique after at least one possession. They can still be lumped into categories, and even their starting category but I like the idea that, kind of like Fallen, rooting in the soul of a human and bargaining for eating their soul (the autonomy system). They touch upon the memories and essence of a human soul, and for the least banes if they eat the autonomy of their host can make a host considerably stronger then their bane of origin.<br /> <br /> I feel say Killing a fomor would be traumatic, but essentially inevitable. Perhaps if the fomori dies from the stress of Possession over time its less traumatic to a bane. But I feel a bane should grow from becoming a Fomor as the Fomor grows. <br /> <br /> There are many many banes so I feel unless being aided by outside sources (either their spirit masters or earther like Pentex) or the bane is intelligent and capable enough, they likely won't get the chance to possess again. Its like if a sperm survives merging with an egg and returns to home base to launch in another mission they likely won't be merging with a second egg due to the massive competition.<br /> <br /> So what are thoughts on the effects for banes? So far I can simulate on a case by case basis, and that would be the ideal way, but I think it would be beneficial to discuss a system. Like Maybe eating Autonomy can raise a banes' traits if they eat more autonomy then the trait they want to increase? And maybe a charm per 3 autonomy eaten? What unique systems to representing being a long lasting Fomor who increases also by Experience, as well as unique Fomors like Psychics, Sorcerers, and Mages?<br /> <br /> And perhaps most interestingly what about Ferectoi which are born as Fomors? Perhaps they actually are like Spirits of the Ferectoi, somewhat like a Wraith or the Misbegotten unborn children of the Mokole.<br /> <br /> Thoughts and suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}